_refine.details                                  
;X-RAY DATA WAS COLLECTED AT -150OC TO MINIMIZE RADIATION
DECAY.  PHASE INFORMATION WAS PROVIDED BY ISOMORPHOUS AND
ANOMALOUS DIFFERENCES MEASURED FOR THE DIMETHYL MERCURY
DERIVATIVE.  EXTENSIVE SOLVENT FLATTENING (B.C. WANG
PROGRAMS) WAS USED TO REFINE THE PHASES PRIOR TO BUILDING
AN ATOMIC MODEL.

THE LOOP CONNECTING THE SECOND AND THIRD HELICES OF THE
FOUR-HELIX BUNDLE (RESIDUES 83-88) IS POORLY DEFINED IN
THE ELECTRON DENSITY MAP.  X-PLOR-REFINED COORDINATES FOR
THE LOOP HAVE BEEN INCLUDED IN THE STRUCTURE BUT ARE LIKELY
TO CONTAIN ERRORS.
;
